sentences.l:
A wonder of beauty, her face the full moon of a star * a dear one of a people, of Zabīb and Rabrab,
the God of the Throne gave her glory and loftiness * and charm and meaning, then a stature slender-cut;
she has in the sky of the face seven stars * on the cheek guards, on every lookout;
if a man sought to steal a glance * devils of speech burned him with a star.

A moon that slays with the glances if he gazes * a branch that crumbles with the stature when he bends,
Zanj-black of the lawāʾib, golden his colour * sweet of the qualities, his stature resembles the lance;
O his before-him, the hard — and the delicacy of his waist * why were you not moved to here from over there?
If the delicacy of his waist were in his heart * he would never have wronged the lover, nor offended;
O my censurer in love of him, be my excuser * who is for me, with a body that wasting has taken possession of?
The fault is only for the heart and my eye * so leave the blame, and leave me in this affliction.
